# Skill Workflow: `{{ slug }}-visual-identity`

Use this skill whenever building UI screens, brand assets, or image prompts for **{{ manifest.project_name }}**.

## Step 1: Wire Design Tokens First
1. Import `tokens.css` (or merge `tailwind.theme.json` / `tokens.w3c.json`) into the project stylesheet before writing components.
2. Inject the Google Fonts stylesheet into the document `<head>`:
   `{{ manifest.typography.google_fonts_import_url }}`

## Step 2: Apply Archetype & Component Geometry
- **Archetype:** {{ manifest.frontend_ui_rules.aesthetic_archetype }}
- **Layout Grid:** {{ manifest.frontend_ui_rules.layout_grid_style }}
- **Buttons:** {{ manifest.frontend_ui_rules.component_guidelines.buttons }}
- **Cards:** {{ manifest.frontend_ui_rules.component_guidelines.cards }}
- **Navigation:** {{ manifest.frontend_ui_rules.component_guidelines.navigation }}
- **Hero Section:** {{ manifest.frontend_ui_rules.component_guidelines.hero_section }}
- **Badges:** {{ manifest.frontend_ui_rules.component_guidelines.badges }}

## Step 3: Generate Cohesive Visual Assets
When invoking an image generator (Midjourney, Flux, Imagen / Nano Banana), always wrap subject prompts with:
- **Prefix:** `{{ manifest.generative_ai_prompts.global_style_prefix }}`
- **Suffix:** `{{ manifest.generative_ai_prompts.global_style_suffix }}`
- **Negative Prompt:** `{{ manifest.generative_ai_prompts.negative_prompt }}`
- **Style Reference Images (`--sref`):** Use `contact_sheet.jpg` or `references/pin_01.jpg`.

## Step 4: Final Visual Audit
Before completing any UI task, verify:
1. Contrast matches WCAG AA (`{{ manifest.color_system.text_primary.hex }}` on `{{ manifest.color_system.background_primary.hex }}`).
2. Surface textures (`{{ manifest.frontend_ui_rules.texture_and_effects | join('; ') }}`) are represented.
3. None of the forbidden patterns appear (`{{ manifest.frontend_ui_rules.anti_patterns | join('; ') }}`).
